# profile.rules — yamlmuster ruleset for SPAR profile front matter.
# Wired in Wave 2b. Translated from validate_profile's vocab walk,
# required-key, yield/star range, and engagement-leak checks; loaded by
# spar::_yamlmuster_profile and driven by spar::validate_profile.
#
# STAYS IMPERATIVE in validate_profile (NOT migrated here): the file read,
# the `---` fence check, the front-matter parse, all three
# invalid_front_matter variants (545-576), and the roster-row comparisons,
# reachability profile_unreachable_without_exclusion (640-651) and
# staleness stale_* (653-678). Those imperative issues are appended AFTER
# the yamlmuster issues, matching their legacy near-last position.
#
# Call shape (design-migration Wave 2b):
#   validate <fm> -groups {profile} -context {raw <raw>} -extra {contact_name <cn>}
# where <fm> is the parsed front-matter dict and <raw> is the whole profile
# text. engagement_leak matches patterns against the `raw` context value.
#
# ORDERING DOUBT (same root cause as approach.rules): legacy runs the vocab
# walk (root then dependent_data) BEFORE the required-key / range /
# engagement_leak rules; yamlmuster fires all root-level rules before
# descending to dependent_data, so `vocab dependent_data` emits AFTER the
# root structural rules rather than right after `vocab root`. DRAFT-NOTES d.

# ── Levels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
level root           -keys {profile_date star_rating yield dependent_data}
level dependent_data -keys {contact_name organisation role date_excluded}

child root dependent_data dict dependent_data

# ── ROOT level rules ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# vocab walk at root. Built-in unknown_key / wrong_level (same wrapper
# rename to unknown_key_<level> as approach). Legacy 579.
rule vocab root -groups {profile}

# Required keys at root: legacy 588-593 (foreach req in this exact order).
# Message template %k = the required key name, reproducing
# "Profile front matter missing required key '<req>'". Existence only.
rule require root profile_date   -code missing_profile_date \
    -message {Profile front matter missing required key '%k'} -groups {profile}
rule require root star_rating    -code missing_star_rating \
    -message {Profile front matter missing required key '%k'} -groups {profile}
rule require root yield          -code missing_yield \
    -message {Profile front matter missing required key '%k'} -groups {profile}
rule require root dependent_data -code missing_dependent_data \
    -message {Profile front matter missing required key '%k'} -groups {profile}

# invalid_yield: legacy 596-602. HOST PREDICATE, not `range`: legacy's guard
# is `[dict exists yield] && (![string is integer -strict $y] || $y < 0)`,
# which fires on a present-but-BLANK yield (a blank is a non-integer). The
# engine's value-reading kinds treat a blank keypath as absent, so `range`
# would let a blank slip through unflagged (and require sees the key as
# present, so no missing_yield either). The predicate replicates the legacy
# guard exactly: skip only when the key is absent; otherwise flag blank and
# non-integer and negative in one check, with the verbatim message.
rule predicate root invalid_yield -code invalid_yield -groups {profile}

# engagement_leak: legacy 604-624. HOST PREDICATE over the `raw` context
# value (the whole profile text), not a front-matter field, so the DSL
# cannot express it and each message interpolates the matched pattern or
# phrase. -needs raw drops it if the caller omits the text. The predicate
# emits, in this order (all code engagement_leak):
#   three case-sensitive `string first` patterns (608-617):
#     "## Prior correspondence" -> "Profile carries a prior-correspondence or warmth section ('## Prior correspondence'). Engagement and pitch content is campaign-bound and must not live in a reusable profile (INVARIANTS.md I1)."
#     "## Angles"               -> "...pitch or angles section ('## Angles')..."
#     "Warmth:"                 -> "...warmth line ('Warmth:')..."
#   three case-insensitive phrases over `string tolower raw` (618-624):
#     "no prior contact" / "no prior correspondence" / "no prior connection"
#       -> "Profile states '<phrase>'. Prior-contact state is campaign-bound and stale on reuse (INVARIANTS.md I1)."
# NOTE: context key name is `raw` per design-migration's call site;
# design-muster called it raw_text (DRAFT-NOTES d).
rule predicate root engagement_leak -needs raw -code engagement_leak \
    -message {Profile carries campaign-bound engagement or pitch content (INVARIANTS.md I1)} \
    -groups {profile}

# invalid_star_rating: legacy 625-631. HOST PREDICATE, same reason as
# invalid_yield: legacy's guard fires on a present-but-BLANK star_rating,
# which the engine's `range` would skip. Emission position AFTER
# engagement_leak, matching legacy order.
rule predicate root invalid_star_rating -code invalid_star_rating -groups {profile}

# ── DEPENDENT_DATA level ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vocab walk: legacy 580-585 (guarded by even-length; -badnode ignore
# reproduces the skip).
rule vocab dependent_data -groups {profile}
